    cases=AUDIT/'COOKING_REVIEW_CASES.md';s=cases.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s=s.replace('Dedicated HP-2 crocks can improve to HP 3 at Standard yield.','Dedicated HP-2 crocks can improve to HP 3 at Standard yield, gaining +1 current HP to preserve the existing damage deficit (2/2 becomes 3/3; 1/2 becomes 2/3).')
    s=s.replace('The four implementation clarifications explicitly submitted with these cases are conservative ingredient edibility credit, supplemental-food incorporation/failure timing, borrowed speed composition with recipient restrictions, and existing dedicated-container damage/durability handling. None is treated as previously exact-reviewed merely because the source conference approved the direction.','The exact GPT review approved these traces after five finite repairs. Supplemental food stays separate until the outcome, then incorporates only the actual finished-product deficit. Borrowed speed replaces the unmodified mode base with max(existing base, donor printed speed), then applies actual modifiers once. Crock improvement preserves damage deficit. Maximum output dispositions allow only one simultaneous immediate meal per actual recipient, with reserved-storage fallback if that arrangement fails. Recipe-120 labels its null source work hours separately from the 1,920-hour overlay.')
